    <div class="tk-prose__body">
      <h2>1. Agreement (Terms of Service)</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Terms of Service</strong></p>
      <p>Welcome to Takebana! By using our platform, including but not limited to live streaming, video content, and any interactive features, you agree to be bound by the following terms and conditions. Please read them carefully before accessing our services.</p>
      <h4>Eligibility</h4>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Minimum Age Requirement:</strong> You must be at least 18 years of age to register, create content, or engage in any live streaming or video content on Takebana. If you are under 18, you are strictly prohibited from using these services.</li>
      <li><strong>Account Creation:</strong> To use certain features, you must create an account, provide accurate information, and maintain confidentiality of your login credentials. You are fully responsible for all activities that occur under your account.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>Live Streaming</h4>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>No Recording Policy:</strong> Takebana <span><strong>does not store, record, or save live streaming sessions</strong></span>. Once the live stream concludes, all content is permanently deleted from our servers. Users are responsible for any personal archiving of their content.</li>
      <li><strong>Content Ownership:</strong> By using the live streaming feature, you acknowledge that you hold the necessary rights to broadcast the content and that the content does not infringe on any third-party rights.</li>
      <li><strong>Prohibited Content:</strong> You may not stream, post, or share content that is:
      <ul>
      <li>Violent, hateful, or promotes illegal activities.</li>
      <li>Discriminatory based on race, religion, gender, nationality, or other protected characteristics.</li>
      <li>Pornographic or sexually explicit.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h4>Modifications</h4>
      <p>Takebana reserves the right to modify these Terms of Service at any time. Continued use of the site signifies your acceptance of any updates.</p>
      <h4>Termination</h4>
      <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account at our discretion for violations of these terms or any applicable law.</p>
      <h2>2. Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Privacy Policy</strong></p>
      <p><strong>Effective Date: [15/09/2024]</strong></p>
      <p>At <strong>Takebana</strong>, we are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring that your personal information is handled safely and responsibly. This Privacy Policy outlines the types of data we collect, how we use it, and the measures we take to protect your information. By using Takebana, you agree to the collection and use of your data as outlined in this policy.</p>
      <h4>1. Information We Collect</h4>
      <p>We collect various types of information to provide and improve our services to you. This includes:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Personal Information:</strong> When you create an account, we collect information such as your name, email address, phone number, date of birth, and any other personal details you provide.</li>
      <li><strong>Device Information:</strong> We collect data about the device you use to access Takebana, including device type, operating system, IP address, device identifiers, and browser type.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> We collect information on how you use Takebana, including the features you interact with, the videos you watch, and the content you create. This also includes the times and dates of your usage.</li>
      <li><strong>Location Information:</strong> When you use location-based features of Takebana, we collect your approximate or precise location, depending on your device settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Third-Party Account Information:</strong> If you link your Takebana account to a third-party platform (such as Facebook or Google), we may collect information from those platforms based on your privacy settings.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>2. How We Use Your Information</h4>
      <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>To Provide Our Services:</strong> Your information helps us to provide and maintain Takebana's functionalities, including live streaming, video sharing, and other interactive features.</li>
      <li><strong>Personalization:</strong> We may use your information to personalize your experience on Takebana, including recommending content, displaying relevant ads, and adjusting the platform's settings to your preferences.</li>
      <li><strong>Communication:</strong> We use your contact information to send you service-related updates, promotional materials, and respond to your inquiries.</li>
      <li><strong>Security:</strong> Your data helps us detect and prevent fraud, abuse, and violations of our terms of service. It also assists us in maintaining the overall security of the platform.</li>
      <li><strong>Compliance with Laws:</strong> We may use your information to comply with applicable legal requirements, court orders, and regulations.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>3. How We Share Your Information</h4>
      <p>We may share your information in the following ways:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>With Service Providers:</strong> We may share your data with trusted third-party service providers who help us operate and maintain Takebana, such as cloud hosting, data analytics, and payment processing.</li>
      <li><strong>With Law Enforcement:</strong> If required by law or in response to a lawful request from public authorities, we may disclose your information to law enforcement or other government bodies.</li>
      <li><strong>With Third-Party Partners:</strong> We may share anonymized or aggregated data with our partners for research, analysis, and marketing purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> If Takebana is involved in a merger, acquisition, or asset sale, your data may be transferred as part of that transaction.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>4. Data Security</h4>
      <p>Takebana takes data security seriously. We implement a variety of security measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. These measures include encryption, access controls, and regular security assessments.</p>
      <p>However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. While we strive to protect your information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.</p>
      <h4>5. Data Retention</h4>
      <p>We retain your personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy, or as required by law. You may request the deletion of your data at any time by contacting us at <strong>privacy@Takebana.com</strong>, and we will process your request in accordance with applicable laws.</p>
      <h4>6. Your Rights</h4>
      <p>You have certain rights regarding your personal information, including the right to:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Access:</strong> You can request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction:</strong> You can request corrections to any inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can request the deletion of your personal data in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> You can request that we limit the processing of your data.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability:</strong> You can request that we transfer your data to another organization.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at <strong>privacy@Takebana.com</strong>. We will respond to your request within a reasonable time frame and in accordance with applicable laws.</p>
      <h4>7. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h4>
      <p>Takebana uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance your user experience and track usage across our platform. These cookies may collect information such as your device type, operating system, and browsing behavior.</p>
      <p>You can manage your cookie preferences through your browser settings. Please note that disabling cookies may impact the functionality of certain Takebana features.</p>
      <h4>8. International Transfers</h4>
      <p>As a global platform, Takebana may transfer your data to countries outside of your home jurisdiction, including the United States and other countries where our service providers operate. We ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place to protect your data during international transfers.</p>
      <h4>9. Children's Privacy</h4>
      <p>Takebana is not intended for users under the age of 18, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a user under 18, we will take steps to delete the information promptly.</p>
      <p>If you believe that we have collected personal information from a minor, please contact us at <strong>privacy@Takebana.com</strong>.</p>
      <h4>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h4>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for legal and regulatory reasons. Any changes will be posted on this page, and we will notify you of any significant changes either through the platform or by email.</p>
      <h4>11. Contact Us</h4>
      <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, or if you would like to exercise your rights regarding your personal data, please contact us at:</p>
      <p>Email: <strong>privacy@Takebana.com</strong></p>
      <p>Mailing Address: <strong>[info@Takebana.com]</strong></p>
      <h2>3. Child Safety Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Child Safety Policy</strong></p>
      <p>I see what you're looking for! Here's a detailed version of the <span><strong>Child Safety Policy</strong></span> for Takebana, closely following the structure you provided, with the necessary adjustments to fit your website:</p>
      <p>At Takebana, the safety and protection of minors is our top priority. We have a zero-tolerance approach to any acts of child sexual exploitation, abuse, or inappropriate sexualization. Any user violating these policies will be immediately removed from the platform, and, where applicable, we will cooperate with law enforcement authorities.</p>
      <h3>Child Sexual Exploitation, Abuse, and Nudity</h3>
      <p>Takebana is committed to providing a safe environment for all users. Below are our specific policies regarding the protection of minors (anyone under the age of 18):</p>
      <h4>Policies</h4>
      <ol>
      <li><strong>Minimum Age Requirement</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>You must be <span><strong>18 years of age or older</strong></span> to register for, use, or participate in any of Takebana’s services, including live streaming and video functionalities.</li>
      <li>If we discover any user under the age of 18 using Takebana’s services, we will take immediate action to remove their account from the platform.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Prohibition of Sexual Exploitation and Abuse</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Sexual exploitation or abuse of minors (anyone under the age of 18) is strictly prohibited. This includes but is not limited to:
      <ul>
      <li>Soliciting minors for sexual purposes.</li>
      <li>Sharing, broadcasting, or engaging in any form of sexual content involving minors.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Mandatory Reporting:</strong> Takebana will report any incidents involving child exploitation or abuse to the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children (NCMEC) or other relevant authorities in accordance with applicable laws. In certain cases, we may also consider evidence of such activity occurring off-platform in determining violations.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Offenders Prohibited from Platform Use</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Users who have been convicted of crimes involving children—including sexual assault, physical abuse, neglect, or trafficking—are strictly prohibited from using Takebana. We take immediate action to remove any such users from the platform upon discovery.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Detection and Prevention of Child Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (CSEA)</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Takebana utilizes both <span><strong>automated systems</strong></span> and <span><strong>manual monitoring</strong></span> to detect underage users as well as any activity related to Child Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (CSEA). These systems help identify illegal or inappropriate content related to minors.</li>
      <li>Attempting to bypass or evade these detection systems is strictly prohibited and may lead to permanent suspension and potential reporting to authorities.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Prohibition of Sexual Fetishization of Minors</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Discussions or acts that sexualize minors are strictly prohibited. This includes, but is not limited to:
      <ul>
      <li>Playacting or engaging in sexualized scenarios involving minors.</li>
      <li>Wearing sexualized clothing or costumes traditionally associated with minors (e.g., schoolgirl uniforms) during live streams or video content.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Child Nudity</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Any form of child nudity is strictly forbidden on Takebana, even in non-sexual or accidental situations. For example, content such as a toddler running from a bath is not allowed, as such images or videos can be misappropriated.</li>
      <li>We strongly recommend avoiding situations that may inadvertently expose a child’s nudity, as such content can be subject to misuse or misinterpretation.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Prohibition on Depictions of Minors in Art Forms</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Takebana prohibits the depiction of child nudity or the fetishization of minors in <span><strong>any form</strong></span>, including drawings, animations, or other creative content. Any such content will be immediately removed from the platform, and violators may face account suspension or legal action.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Prohibition on Violence Against Children</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Any engagement in, encouragement of, or threats involving <span><strong>physical violence against children</strong></span> is strictly prohibited. Users are not permitted to broadcast or share content depicting violence or harm to minors in any form, and such behavior will result in immediate action.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h4>Reporting Violations</h4>
      <p>If you become aware of any violations of these policies, including the presence of child exploitation or abuse, you are encouraged to report the incident immediately using the <span><strong>in-app reporting system</strong></span> or by contacting us at [email]. Takebana takes these reports seriously and will act promptly to investigate and address any violations. Depending on the nature of the violation, we may also involve law enforcement authorities.</p>
      <h4>Resources</h4>
      <p>In addition to reporting child exploitation or abuse through Takebana’s channels, we encourage you to report such incidents to the appropriate authorities in your region:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>North America, Australia, New Zealand:</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Contact the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children (NCMEC) <a href="https://www.missingkids.org/" target="_blank">https://www.missingkids.org/</a></li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Europe:</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Law Enforcement Reporting Channels for Child Sexual Coercion and Extortion.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>South America and Other Regions:</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Contact the <span><strong>International Centre for Missing & Exploited Children (ICMEC)</strong></span> <a href="https://www.icmec.org/global-missing-childrens-center/" target="_blank">https://www.icmec.org/global-missing-childrens-center/</a></li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>4. Anti-Bullying and Harassment Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Anti-Bullying Policy</strong></p>
      <p>At Takebana, we believe in fostering a positive and respectful community. Harassment, bullying, or any form of abusive behavior will not be tolerated.</p>
      <h4>Prohibited Behavior</h4>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Bullying:</strong> This includes repeated intimidation, threats, or public shaming.</li>
      <li><strong>Harassment:</strong> This includes any unwanted or inappropriate behavior based on gender, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, or sexual orientation.</li>
      <li><strong>Stalking:</strong> Tracking or harassing users both online and offline is strictly prohibited.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>Zero Tolerance</h4>
      <p>Users who engage in bullying or harassment will be subject to immediate account suspension or termination without warning. Reports of bullying will be thoroughly investigated, even though <span><strong>live streams are not recorded</strong></span>. User complaints and feedback will be key in resolving disputes.</p>
      <h4>Reporting</h4>
      <p>You can report incidents of bullying or harassment to our support team at [email]. We ensure prompt and discreet handling of all complaints.</p>
      <h2>5. Cookie Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Cookie Policy</strong></p>
      <p>Takebana uses cookies to ensure a better user experience. Cookies enable us to improve service performance, remember user preferences, and provide relevant content.</p>
      <h4>Types of Cookies</h4>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> These enable the core functionality of the website.</li>
      <li><strong>Performance Cookies:</strong> These help us analyze and understand how users interact with Takebana.</li>
      <li><strong>Marketing Cookies:</strong> These deliver personalized advertisements based on your preferences.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>Cookie Management</h4>
      <p>You can manage or block cookies through your browser settings. However, please note that disabling cookies may impact the functionality of certain features, including live streaming.</p>
      <h2>6. Legal Inquiry Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Legal Inquiry Policy</strong></p>
      <p>If you have any legal inquiries, including requests related to law enforcement, intellectual property, or user disputes, please contact us at [email].</p>
      <h4>Contact Information</h4>
      <p>All legal inquiries must be submitted in writing, including the specific nature of the request, relevant legal documentation, and contact details. We aim to respond to all requests within 10 business days.</p>
      <h2>7. Copyright Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Takebana Copyright Policy</strong></p>
      <p>Takebana respects the intellectual property of others and requires that users do the same.</p>
      <h4>Infringement and Reporting</h4>
      <p>If you believe that your copyright has been infringed by content shared on Takebana, please provide:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>A detailed description of the copyrighted work.</li>
      <li>The location of the infringing content (e.g., profile name, stream time).</li>
      <li>Proof of ownership.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Since <span><strong>live streams are not stored</strong></span>, we rely on real-time reporting and action. Users are expected to avoid copyright infringement during live sessions.</p>
      <h4>Consequences of Violation</h4>
      <p>Takebana reserves the right to terminate the accounts of users who repeatedly infringe on intellectual property rights.</p>
